# AILocators Naming Convention

## File Naming
Format: `{DescriptiveName}-{ElementType}.rs`

## Element Type Suffixes
| Suffix | Element Type |
|--------|-------------|
| `-Btn` | Buttons (clickable actions) |
| `-Link` | Navigation links |
| `-Tab` | Tab elements |
| `-Ddn` | Dropdowns / Select elements |
| `-Ddn-Option` | Dropdown option items |
| `-Ddn-Input` | Dropdown input/search field |
| `-TxtBx` | Text inputs |
| `-RadioBtn` | Radio buttons |
| `-Chkbx` | Checkboxes |
| `-Switch` | Toggle switches |
| `-Lbl` | Labels / display text |
| `-Row` | Table rows |
| `-Header` | Table column headers |
| `-Icon` | Icon buttons or status icons |
| `-Tooltip` | Tooltips |
| `-Dialog` | Dialog/modal containers |
| `-Alert` | Alert components |
| `-Cell` | Table cells |
| `-Chip` | Status chips |
| `-Form` | Form containers |
| `-Container` | Wrapper elements |

## Naming Rules
- PascalCase for multi-word names: `SubmissionName-TxtBx`, `DataCommons-Ddn`
- Names match UI labels where possible
- Dynamic elements use index placeholder in name: `AdditionalContact-0-FirstName-TxtBx`

## XPath Locator Priority
1. `//*[@data-testid='value']` — Prefer when available
2. `//*[@id='value']` — For elements with stable IDs
3. `//*[@aria-label='value']` — For accessible elements
4. `//button[.='Text']` or `//a[.='Text']` — Text content match
5. `//*[contains(@class,'MuiComponent')]` — MUI class (last resort)

## Referencing AILocators in Scripts
```groovy
// Path format: CRDC/AILocators/{Page}/{SubPage}/{LocatorName}
findTestObject('CRDC/AILocators/DataSubmissions/List/Filters/Program-Ddn')
findTestObject('CRDC/AILocators/Global/Header/Desktop/DataSubmissions-Tab')
findTestObject('CRDC/AILocators/SubmissionRequests/Form/SectionA/PI-FirstName-TxtBx')
```
